# PDFs are binary. Without this, a PDF whose bytes happen to contain no NUL in
# the first 8k (an uncompressed one, for instance) is auto-detected as text and
# gets CRLF line-ending conversion applied under core.autocrlf=true — which
# rewrites bytes inside the file and invalidates its xref offsets, leaving a
# PDF that no longer opens. Marking them binary disables both conversion and
# textual diffing.
*.pdf binary
